\subsection{Plasma Diagnostics}
\noindent
Real-time closed-loop control of the ${}^{11}\text{B}$--D fusion core and
positron/antiproton annihilation stream is achieved through a tri-modal
diagnostic suite.

\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Thomson Scattering Arrays:}
    Nd:YAG laser scattering for electron temperature $T_e$ and density $n_e$ mapping.
    \item \textbf{Neutron and Alpha Spectrometers:}
    Fast scintillation detectors for fusion yield and real-time gain scaling ($Q = 320$).
    \item \textbf{Mirnov Coil Matrices:}
    High-frequency magnetic pickup coils embedded in CNT walls for MHD instability detection.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Orbital Test Telemetry Framework}
\noindent
During TRL 6--8 orbital validation, telemetry is streamed via encrypted
Ka-band downlinks.

\begin{lemma}[Telemetry Rate]
The AITFE telemetry architecture supports a nominal logging rate of
$200\ \text{Hz}$, enabling sub-millisecond detection of thermal transients
and injection throttling ($\pm 15\%$).
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
The Ka-band downlink bandwidth exceeds the required data throughput for
high-frequency plasma diagnostics, thrust vectoring logs, and thermal
profiles. Thus the stated rate is achievable within standard orbital
communication envelopes.
\end{proof}

\subsection{Safety and Containment Protocols}
\noindent
The Cryogenic Antimatter Storage Subsystem (CASS) integrates triple-redundant
containment layers.

\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Primary Penning--Malmberg Trap:}
    Ultra-high vacuum ($<10^{-12}$ torr) and $9\ \text{T}$ superconducting
    magnetic confinement.
    \item \textbf{Secondary Cryogenic Shielding:}
    He-3 closed-loop refrigeration at $4\ \text{K}$ for thermal isolation.
    \item \textbf{Tertiary Passive Annihilation Dump (PAD):}
    Pyrolytic graphite and WC absorbers engineered to dissipate stored
    rest-mass energy ($125.8\ \text{GW}$ equivalent) under emergency quench.
\end{enumerate}

